    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as the clear alpha, boasting a massive 84.82 score. His matchup against Canning is ideal; between the plus-matchup against a 4.76 xERA starter and the significant platoon advantage, he is primed to bolster our scarcest category, stolen bases. **Seiya Suzuki** also draws a premium assignment with a 73.90 rating. He benefits from a +16% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against the left-handed Triston Rogers, where his ability to exploit a slow delivery increases his stolen base ceiling, making him our second most efficient outfield engine behind **Corbin Carroll**.\n\nThe most contentious decision today was relegating **Jose Caballero** to the bench with a 39.32 score. Despite his utility value, the combination of an elite matchup against Rasmussen and a negative platoon split pushed him just beneath our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor. We prioritized the stability of **Austin Riley** at 62.88, as his superior SP-skill matchup (+17%) and reliability in the #7 hole offered a safer floor for plate appearances compared to the riskier profile of **Jose Caballero**. We are keeping a close watch on **Cole Young**; at 47.41, he is hovering near the danger zone, and any further shift in the lineup order or a late scratch could necessitate a pivot toward our deeper bench assets like **Mickey Moniak** or **Giancarlo Stanton** if they were available for substitution.\n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly for **Zach McKinstry**, who is dealing with an elite defensive catcher (1.89s pop time) that slightly caps his stolen base upside against Suarez. While **Henry Bolte** and **Travis Bazzana** provide necessary depth, their scores are anchored by lower-order placement. We are effectively betting that the volume against mid-tier arms like Junk and Ober will outweigh the lack of premium lineup spots for the lower half of the roster. Ensure all roster locks are monitored, especially for **Tyler Soderstrom** and **James Wood**, who remain on the bench today due to their lack of active status in the confirmed lineups.",
